---
/**
 * Overrides the `th` element inside article MDX, purely to add `scope="col"`.
 *
 * A markdown table gives its header cells no scope, so an assistive technology
 * has to guess which column a cell belongs to. On the osteoporosis medicines
 * table that guess is the whole content: column three is "tell your doctor if",
 * and a value read without its header is a warning with nothing attached to it.
 * WCAG 2.2 AA asks for the association (1.3.1 Info and Relationships).
 *
 * `col` is right for every table on the site and will stay right, because
 * markdown has no syntax for a row header: a `<th>` can only ever appear in the
 * header row. If a hand-written table ever needs `scope="row"`, it cannot use
 * this override.
 *
 * Done as an MDX component override for the same reason `Table.astro` is — see
 * the note there about Astro 7's Markdown processor and rehype plugins.
 */
---

<th scope="col"><slot /></th>
